WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.660
<b>At Sea in the New World</b>

3
00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.870
I'm so hungry!

4
00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:03.420
What's this junk?

5
00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:07.210
Whoa, where did you get that?

6
00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:09.800
Uhh. It wound up in my pocket somehow.

7
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:11.800
Holy crap! Is it real?

8
00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.050
Why, what is it anyway?

9
00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:14.100
Don't you remember?

10
00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:18.340
Germa used 'em to do
those cool transformations!

11
00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:20.140
Oh! So that's it!

12
00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:22.390
Lemme me give that thing a quick spin!

13
00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:24.350
I'm goin' before you!

14
00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:27.020
– Sanji!
– Sanji!

15
00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.360
I'm gonna chuck this hunka garbage.

16
00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:32.940
Don't throw it away!

17
00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:36.020
If you do, I'm gonna dive to the
bottom of the sea to find it!

18
00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:38.570
Good luck with that! You can't swim!

19
00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:42.710
It was in my pocket, so if you don't
want it, just give it back to me instead!

20
00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:44.930
I'll gladly take it off your hands!

21
00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:45.970
Get lost.

22
00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:51.270
I am rather curious as to how it
wandered into Luffy's pocket, somehow.

23
00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:53.690
It musta been Niji!

24
00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:55.690
He probably did it to piss me off.

25
00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:01.030
If I'm gonna get stronger,
I won't do it

26
00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:03.160
by relying on this thing
or some technological crap.

27
00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:04.870
Just put it down, please!

28
00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:07.640
Science is the power of mankind itself!

29
00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:09.640
What do you guys want it for?

30
00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:12.600
– If you let us put the raid suit on...
– If you let us put the raid suit on...

31
00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:21.180
– Maybe we can shoot laser beams!
– Maybe we can shoot laser beams!

32
00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:22.600
What are you guys, ten years old?

33
00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:26.670
Besides, Franky's got enough
lasers and crap for the whole crew!

34
00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:27.960
No! I want it!

35
00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.760
What was that? Did you insult science?

36
00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.740
Nami! Why, perish the thought!

37
00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:36.260
I think science is lovely!

38
00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:40.100
My Sorcerer's Clima Tact was made from
atmospheric science and the craftsmanship

39
00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:42.310
of our own Usopp, you know!

40
00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:43.640
Now, out!

41
00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:50.680
I'm really lovin'
life in that baton!

42
00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:53.770
Zeus! You actually tagged along?

43
00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:57.040
I can't believe you chose your
stomach over loyalty to Big Mom!

44
00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.210
He's quite the
useful servant, isn't he?

45
00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:00.920
He's your what, Nami?

46
00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:03.730
Oh yeah? Zeus, just so you know,

47
00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:08.360
I've been Nami's devoted servant
long before you showed up, okay?

48
00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:12.070
I mean, that's cute and all,
but I get to live inside her baton,

49
00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:13.440
which never leaves her side.

50
00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:17.900
Sanji, you're yelling
at a mass of water vapor.

51
00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:19.980
Germa! Let's power up!

52
00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:23.650
– Where the heck's my cool suit?
– Where the heck's my cool suit?

53
00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:24.990
Stop your crying!

54
00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:27.120
I guess the thing only works
when you do it, huh?

55
00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:31.990
Shut up! I'm not part of
that goon squad!

56
00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:33.330
New rules!

57
00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.870
Don't say the word
"Vinsmoke" or "Germa" either!

58
00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:38.460
They're officially off limits
anytime you're around me!

59
00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.200
Thanks, pal!

60
00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:44.700
Just show us how to do it one
time and we'll leave you alone!

61
00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.450
Guys! The newspaper's here!

62
00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:50.000
Is there any coverage
about us crashing the wedding?

63
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.340
Let's see.

64
00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:54.590
Luffy's on the front page!

65
00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:56.030
What about Jimbei?

66
00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:58.120
Does it say if he
made it out okay, or...?

67
00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:01.870
Um, Jimbei, Jimbei.

68
00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:04.290
No, I don't see anything.

69
00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:09.630
It says Luffy, Sanji, Jimbei,
and Bege attempted to assassinate Big Mom,

70
00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:11.840
and you-teia were the mastermind!

71
00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:12.920
"Mastermind"?

72
00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:15.800
Look, Sanji!

73
00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:21.370
My bounty increased
to 330 million berries?

74
00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:23.100
No frickin' way!

75
00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.260
Huh? What's Moss-head sitting at?

76
00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:27.390
That should put him
right below you now.

77
00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:29.600
He has a 320 million bounty.

78
00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:34.280
Hell yeah! In your face, jackass!

79
00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:36.110
It's just a number, don't flip out.

80
00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:38.030
And they change it from "live only"

81
00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:40.240
back to "dead or alive"!

82
00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:45.870
Sanji? What's the matter?

83
00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:47.310
My name.

84
00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:49.920
– Huh?
– Huh?

85
00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:53.940
It changed to "Vinsmoke Sanji"!

86
00:04:53.940 --> 00:05:03.200
<b>GLOOM...</b>

87
00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:59.880
Dammit, it was only increased
because of my family's reputation.

88
00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:02.700
Sanji, buddy? You gonna be all right?

89
00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:06.370
It's somehow
even gloomier over there!

90
00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:08.580
<b>GLOOM...</b>

91
00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:09.660
<b>DOOM...</b>

92
00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:11.670
Luffy! What's the problem?

93
00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:14.460
<b>The Fifth Emperor</b>

94
00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.730
Meanwhile, everyone is abuzz

95
00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:23.900
about the upcoming Reverie, a conference
made up of all the world's leaders.

96
00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:29.120
It takes place in the Holy Land
of Mary Geoise once every four years.

97
00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:34.650
This is Fishman Island, located
10,000 meters below sea level.

98
00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:37.610
It's home of the Ryugu Kingdom.

99
00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:39.820
They did it-jamon!

100
00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:43.110
Jimbei has finally joined Luffy's crew!

101
00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:49.560
It's hard to believe that the two of them
picked a fight with Big Mom herself.

102
00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:49.540
<b>King Neptune
Ryugu Kingdom</b>

103
00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:52.460
Do you suppose they were all
able to escape on the same ship?

104
00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:55.410
<b>Ryuboshi Manboshi</b>

105
00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:55.380
I certainly hope so-la-ti-do!

106
00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:58.120
<b>Fukuboshi Ryuboshi Manboshi</b>

107
00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.380
Surely they did.

108
00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:00.090
In the article, it mentions
that Big Mom is furious.

109
00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:00.000
<b>Fukuboshi Ryuboshi</b>

110
00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:05.130
I don't think Big Mom will be so
keen to protect our country anymore.

111
00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:07.430
We'll have to see if
Straw Hat will do it.

112
00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:10.140
Don't leave yet! Father!

113
00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:14.100
Shirahoshi!

114
00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:17.900
<b>Princess Shirahoshi</b>

115
00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.770
I'm coming with you!

116
00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:18.020
To the Reverie!

117
00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:22.810
If I go, Luffy won't be able to pick
on me for being a scaredy cat anymore!

118
00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:29.480
I was hoping
you would find the courage.

119
00:06:29.850 --> 00:06:31.480
All right, are you ready?

120
00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:33.650
Uh-huh!

121
00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:39.520
Though the meeting of world
leaders is certainly big news,

122
00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:43.270
word of Luffy's bold adventures seems
to be the only thing on anyone's mind.

123
00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:46.350
The story about a young pirate
who took a stand against

124
00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:48.490
the untouchable Emperor
of the Sea, Big Mom,

125
00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:51.290
thrills all who hear it,
across the world.

126
00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:53.920
The newspaper states:

127
00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:56.270
"Sources report that Straw Hat Luffy

128
00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:58.270
is already in control of
seven powerful pirate crews

129
00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:01.490
that he's recruited along the way.

130
00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:04.130
This makes him the captain of a fleet

131
00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:06.890
that has a combined total of
over 5,000 fearsome pirates.

132
00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:10.180
He's not only the
sworn brother of the late Ace,

133
00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:13.980
but also Sabo, Second-in-Command
of the Revolutionary Army.

134
00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:17.560
His natural magnetism
and leadership skills

135
00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:21.070
have drawn the evil army,
Germa 66, to his side,

136
00:07:21.070 --> 00:07:25.410
along with the Sun Pirates, and
the Firetank Pirates as well."

137
00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:28.320
"His plan to destroy Big Mom's castle

138
00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:31.200
can only be seen as a work
of strategic brilliance.

139
00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:36.540
Additionally, he defeated her highest-ranked
officers with sheer strength alone.

140
00:07:37.110 --> 00:07:38.690
The outcome of this battle
clearly confirms that

141
00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:41.360
Straw Hat Luffy is
a force to be reckoned with."

142
00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:45.310
And the last line of the article
makes a bold statement.

143
00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:49.870
"The fifth Emperor
of the Sea has emerged!"

144
00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:54.740
Are you kidding?

145
00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.660
What's this "Fifth Emperor" bullcrap?

146
00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.830
The press must have
lost their damn minds,

147
00:07:57.160 --> 00:08:02.170
<b>Fleet Admiral Sakazuki
Marine Headquarters</b>

148
00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:02.330
giving such a lavish title
to a little upstart like him.

149
00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:09.250
Fleet Admiral! We have a problem!

150
00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:10.870
The Kingdom of Lulucia's ship that was

151
00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:13.270
en route to the Reverie
has been attacked by pirates!

152
00:08:14.020 --> 00:08:18.310
The king was unharmed,
but Princess Comane has been kidnapped.

153
00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:20.940
What was the point of an armed escort?

154
00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:32.860
Grandfather! Grandfather!

155
00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:34.860
Hm? Rebecca? What's wrong?

156
00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:36.030
Look! The front page!

157
00:08:35.540 --> 00:08:40.790
“Assassins Make Attempt on Big Mom's Life"

158
00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:38.530
It's all about Lucy!

159
00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:41.330
<b>Rebecca
A Dressrosan Lady-in-Waiting</b>

160
00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:40.330
Yes, I saw!

161
00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:41.450
Okay.

162
00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:43.830
I'm so proud! That's our captain!

163
00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:46.580
Luffyland is even more famous now!

164
00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:50.650
And it's kinda cool how the
newspaper mentions all of us, too!

165
00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:51.390
<b>Commander Leo
Tonta Corps, Tontatta Tribe</b>

166
00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:52.070
Don't forget.

167
00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:56.580
Once we arrive, Leo, you cannot
bring up such matters.

168
00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:58.500
Huh? Why can't we, though?

169
00:08:58.500 --> 00:08:59.530
It's quite simple.

170
00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:01.200
We owe a great debt to the Straw Hats,

171
00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:04.200
but the Government
sees them in a different way.

172
00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:05.600
Let's keep that in mind.

173
00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:07.770
You're right! They are pirates!

174
00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:12.160
Straw Hat Luffy is considered
a dangerous man.

175
00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:13.870
Best to avoid trouble.

176
00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:15.210
I suppose so.

177
00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:17.880
Oh yeah! I should show this to Viola!

178
00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:20.520
Hey! Wait for us!

179
00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:25.300
There's no mistaking it.

180
00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:28.510
Those ships are from the
Dressrosa and Prodence Kingdoms!

181
00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:30.840
And not a Marine in sight!

182
00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:33.640
Oh! I-It's Princess Viola!

183
00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:35.680
She's just as stunning as they say!

184
00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:39.010
The girl she's with is also
a royal family member, I think?

185
00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:40.350
If we can kidnap these two,

186
00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:44.070
I wonder how much
we get for 'em!

187
00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:46.120
Agreed? Princess Comane?

188
00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:49.170
Please, just get ahold
of my pa already!

189
00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:52.630
I know that he'll be willing
to pay you as much as you want!

190
00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:56.550
This is why
I love nabbing royalty!

191
00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:58.270
Hold out for a few more.

192
00:09:58.270 --> 00:10:00.340
Let's make that ransom real hefty!

193
00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:02.090
Those suckers can't spot us.

194
00:10:02.090 --> 00:10:03.300
They can't catch us.

195
00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:04.970
And they'll never see us coming!

196
00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:07.970
Gentlemen, I love this submarine!

197
00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:09.010
Sink 'em!

198
00:10:09.010 --> 00:10:10.180
Roger!

199
00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:19.270
Huh?

200
00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:37.870
Oh, no!

201
00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:41.460
An attack? Ready the cannons!

202
00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:44.210
Yes, sir!

203
00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:46.380
Not necessary.

204
00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:51.920
Glad I made it in time!

205
00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:53.590
You're all safe now!

206
00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:55.220
A-Are you a Marine?

207
00:10:56.550 --> 00:11:00.560
<b>Captain Koby
Marine Headquarters</b>

208
00:10:57.060 --> 00:11:00.690
A Captain from HQ. I'm Koby!

209
00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:02.150
Did it miss the target?

210
00:11:02.150 --> 00:11:04.110
There's no way!

211
00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:11.010
Did anyone get hurt?

212
00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:18.060
Heh. Your parties are from Dressrosa
and Prodence, isn't that correct?

213
00:11:18.060 --> 00:11:20.260
Long way! You must be tired!

214
00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:22.300
Huh? What just happened?

215
00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:24.640
Oh, my. Where did you come from?

216
00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:30.000
I was patrolling on that Navy ship.

217
00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:35.330
Y'know, you folks were being
stalked by some pirates just now.

218
00:11:35.330 --> 00:11:37.950
-Underwater. -Under the surface?

219
00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:39.710
Was it a torpedo?

220
00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:41.530
I'm sure glad they missed us.

221
00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:44.530
Me, too.

222
00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:46.790
Helmeppo. How goes it?

223
00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:49.160
We've got the pirates under control!

224
00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:54.610
Look!

225
00:11:54.740 --> 00:11:58.740
<b>Lieutenant Commander Helmeppo
Marine Headquarters</b>

226
00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:57.970
The Lulucia Princess, Comane, is fine.

227
00:11:57.970 --> 00:12:00.390
Roast these bastards on a skewer!

228
00:12:00.390 --> 00:12:01.480
You'll suffer!

229
00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:02.850
Just wait, you monsters!

230
00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:04.110
Let's calm down!

231
00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:06.030
We'll handle them. Easy now!

232
00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:10.530
I still don't get how your Observation
Haki is so in tune, Koby. Crazy.

233
00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:14.320
I wasn't able to sense
the torpedo at all.

234
00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:18.190
A submarine?

235
00:12:18.190 --> 00:12:20.570
You have to be careful
with pirates these days.

236
00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:22.650
That was a bit too close.

237
00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:23.820
You there!

238
00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:28.200
The famous Captain Koby, I presume?

239
00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:30.800
Huh? So is he the one from Rocky Port?

240
00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:33.620
So you were the Marine
from the incident?

241
00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:37.500
The one perpetrated by Trafalgar
Law of the Worst Generation?

242
00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:38.920
Incredible!

243
00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:41.630
This hero protected all those people!

244
00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:45.500
Oh, I'm hardly a hero. It's nothing!

245
00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:47.210
So you're not only daring.

246
00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:48.820
But you're humble, too!

247
00:12:48.820 --> 00:12:51.580
Wow. This guy looks tough!

248
00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:53.540
What a fine lad.

249
00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:55.960
If only he could take a compliment.

250
00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:57.680
Thank you!

251
00:12:57.680 --> 00:12:58.680
Thanks!

252
00:12:58.680 --> 00:13:00.380
Luffy? No way!

253
00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:02.050
-Huh? -Oh, sorry!

254
00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:05.760
I mean, I just noticed the headline
in the newspaper you're holding!

255
00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:07.430
Here, take it!

256
00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:10.890
No, no!
Well, I mean, if you don't mind.

257
00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:16.690
"The Fifth Emperor of
the Sea has emerged!"

258
00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:19.190
I'm so proud of him!

259
00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:21.230
He's so cool!

260
00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:25.150
He keeps reaching higher and higher.

261
00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:27.660
Uh? Hey.

262
00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:36.550
Every time I see you in the newspaper,
I think back to that day.

263
00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:43.040
Captain Koby! What're you doing?

264
00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:44.500
Come on back!

265
00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:45.670
Yes, sir!

266
00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:53.590
Thank you. I appreciate it!

267
00:13:54.550 --> 00:13:56.090
Okay, let's go.

268
00:13:56.090 --> 00:13:57.830
We're nearly to New Marineford.

269
00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:02.430
The Navy would be happy to escort
you the rest of the way there.

270
00:14:02.430 --> 00:14:04.350
Good. Let's go.

271
00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:06.840
Psst. Hey!

272
00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:09.180
What is it?

273
00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:11.560
Lucy's your friend, isn't he?

274
00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:13.560
Koby! You like Luffyland?

275
00:14:14.020 --> 00:14:15.940
Nuh-uh! He's a foe!

276
00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:17.400
Yeah right.

277
00:14:17.930 --> 00:14:19.740
Don't worry, we won't tell.

278
00:14:19.740 --> 00:14:21.320
I think we should have a little talk!

279
00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:22.700
I'm a Navy Officer!

280
00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:25.280
A-And I need to get going!

281
00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:28.120
But you looked so happy when
you were reading the paper.

282
00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:30.290
Th-That's because I, uh...

283
00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:31.460
Come on. Let's talk!

284
00:14:31.460 --> 00:14:32.920
No! Please stop!

285
00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:35.630
Oh, Luffyland's in this article, too!

286
00:14:36.460 --> 00:14:38.170
So you are his friend!

287
00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:50.620
Damn. My bounty only increased

288
00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:52.290
bad rep.

289
00:14:52.540 --> 00:14:58.550
That takes all the fun out of it.

290
00:14:58.550 --> 00:15:00.840
Hey, uh. Are you okay?

291
00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:03.100
Luffy, are you in pain?

292
00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:07.430
N-No, it's just. Look.

293
00:15:07.430 --> 00:15:08.850
– Huh?
– Huh?

294
00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:12.600
My bounty's gone down!

295
00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:14.100
Y'see?

296
00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:16.140
It's 150 million.

297
00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:16.840
– Huh?
– Huh?

298
00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:17.890
Are you sure?

299
00:15:20.220 --> 00:15:23.100
Wasn't it 500? A while back?

300
00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:24.810
That went down by a whole lot.

301
00:15:24.810 --> 00:15:27.060
It's even lower than
it was two years ago!

302
00:15:27.060 --> 00:15:29.320
How is that possible?

303
00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:32.030
Did you do something wrong, perhaps?

304
00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:33.080
Isn't that backwards?

305
00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:36.590
Ah, yes. You're right.

306
00:15:37.980 --> 00:15:39.140
No biggie!

307
00:15:39.140 --> 00:15:41.270
Less people will be
after your head now!

308
00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:43.400
Nami, how could you say that?

309
00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:44.650
Luffy is our captain!

310
00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:46.240
It could harm our prestige!

311
00:15:46.240 --> 00:15:49.590
Dammit! Why?

312
00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:53.890
<b>A Port Town
Kingdom of Lulusia, Grand Line</b>

313
00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:53.890
Ready the cannons! And fire!

314
00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:01.270
Let's go!

315
00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:04.980
Grab anything not tied down!

316
00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:07.570
What the hell is the Navy doing?

317
00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:09.990
I thought they were here to protect us!

318
00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:13.990
You'll pay for destroying our ship!

319
00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:16.950
Take him out!

320
00:16:22.470 --> 00:16:26.350
The Navy's just a joke!

321
00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:27.890
Lucky us!

322
00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:29.570
The Lulucia King is
away for the Reverie,

323
00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:33.160
and he took all his
best soldiers with him!

324
00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:38.120
For pirates like me, an unguarded country
like this is ripe for the picking.

325
00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:41.830
Now listen up, and listen well!

326
00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:46.520
Have you ever heard of the Emperor
of the Sea "Blackbeard"?

327
00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:52.570
<b>Captain Pinkbeard
Pinkbeard Pirates
Bounty: 52 Million</b>

328
00:16:46.870 --> 00:16:50.080
I work under him, and I've
taken on the name "Peachbeard."

329
00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:52.710
You would do well to remember it!

330
00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:55.120
Fear Blackbeard!

331
00:16:55.510 --> 00:16:56.840
All right, gentlemen.

332
00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:02.640
Let's start loading up the ships
and make our leader proud, shall we?

333
00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:04.560
Gotcha!

334
00:17:10.290 --> 00:17:11.840
Now empty those pockets!

335
00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:14.050
Okay. Just get off of me.

336
00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:16.880
It's no use trying to get away!

337
00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:19.010
We'll burn this whole place down!

338
00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:24.860
Can you stand?
Let's get you out of here!

339
00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:34.110
Huh? Hey, you better not
let that girl escape!

340
00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:36.900
Not so fast!

341
00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:41.950
What's that you got there, missy?

342
00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:45.710
Now what in the world
could be so precious

343
00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:47.290
that you would dare
try and hide it from me?

344
00:17:48.470 --> 00:17:49.420
Sorry, sir.

345
00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:51.670
Huh? Is that milk?

346
00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:54.050
I thought it would be money.

347
00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:56.430
No big deal, I'll take it anyway.

348
00:17:56.800 --> 00:18:00.500
Please, mister. This is for
the children of the village.

349
00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:01.540
Ah, shut it!

350
00:18:07.510 --> 00:18:10.300
You're really willing to
risk your life for some milk?

351
00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:15.070
Please give it back to me.

352
00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:16.640
I beg of you.

353
00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:19.270
It's not much, but we need it.

354
00:18:19.270 --> 00:18:22.940
Huh? Why don't you
hand over your money, too?

355
00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:25.210
I don't have any.

356
00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:28.610
I bet you have your
heavenly tribute, though.

357
00:18:28.610 --> 00:18:31.990
Yes, but the heavenly tribute

358
00:18:31.990 --> 00:18:34.410
is what we have to pay to the
king and the Celestial Dragons.

359
00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:36.620
We're barely getting by as-is.

360
00:18:36.620 --> 00:18:39.290
It takes every last berry
we can scrape together.

361
00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:43.170
If we can't pay the Heavenly
Tribute, we'll be put to death!

362
00:18:43.170 --> 00:18:46.760
What a shame.
Your king sounds terrible!

363
00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:48.630
I guess I have no choice!

364
00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:52.540
You fellas know what to do!

365
00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:55.710
Rip this town apart, and find
where they hid the money!

366
00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:58.130
It's gotta be somewhere!

367
00:18:58.130 --> 00:18:59.730
-We're gonna be rich! -Please don't!

368
00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:02.910
Tell us. Where's the
Tribute stashed away?

369
00:19:03.270 --> 00:19:06.330
Just leave us alone.
Our town has nothing.

370
00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:08.630
Please don't take this
money, it's all I have!

371
00:19:08.630 --> 00:19:09.710
Get your grubby hands off!

372
00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:12.760
Someone help!

373
00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:16.590
You wouldn't have gotten beaten
if you gave us what we wanted!

374
00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:18.800
Kill everyone who disobeys!

375
00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:24.900
We've suffered enough.
Please, leave our people alone!

376
00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:26.770
Huh? Shut your trap!

377
00:19:30.510 --> 00:19:32.520
Morley. Let's do this.

378
00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:35.990
Hm? And just who the hell are you?

379
00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:40.120
Why is the ground shaking?

380
00:19:50.030 --> 00:19:52.120
Something is coming up from the street?

381
00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:01.760
What the hell?

382
00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:04.090
Why's a huge-ass trident here?

383
00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:12.520
Hm? Is that a Giant?

384
00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:18.360
One, two! One, two!

385
00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:29.030
What the hell was this
huge guy doing underground?

386
00:20:29.030 --> 00:20:31.280
That's, uh, some outfit, man!

387
00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:34.750
Uh. Why is he wearing a miniskirt?

388
00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:40.380
Don't be a creep!
Watch where you're lookin'!

389
00:20:43.910 --> 00:20:46.330
Hey, buddy, my eyes are up here!

390
00:20:46.750 --> 00:20:49.710
If you're that into me,
then just say it, bro!

391
00:20:50.080 --> 00:20:52.000
Where did you get that idea?

392
00:20:52.340 --> 00:20:54.500
Those are some mighty
tall accusations there!

393
00:20:55.040 --> 00:20:56.370
I've had enough of you!

394
00:20:56.370 --> 00:20:57.750
Just shoot this guy!

395
00:20:57.750 --> 00:20:59.040
Huh?

396
00:21:00.170 --> 00:21:02.880
You little boys should leave me alone!

397
00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:09.410
So, since when
do Giants live underground?

398
00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:10.970
I've never seen one before.

399
00:21:11.390 --> 00:21:13.020
I wonder who this guy is.

400
00:21:13.470 --> 00:21:15.980
Big old meanies like you
will be punished!

401
00:21:16.730 --> 00:21:18.230
Let's go!

402
00:21:18.820 --> 00:21:21.700
How is this guy pushing
the road around like it's clay?

403
00:21:21.700 --> 00:21:24.290
Don't back down!
It's only a devil fruit!

404
00:21:25.210 --> 00:21:26.160
He's so tough.

405
00:21:26.540 --> 00:21:29.130
So. What do you wanna do?

406
00:21:29.130 --> 00:21:30.420
Huh?

407
00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:34.060
You submissive pieces of trash.

408
00:21:34.420 --> 00:21:35.500
Hey, that's rude.

409
00:21:36.470 --> 00:21:38.010
What do you suggest we do?

410
00:21:38.760 --> 00:21:42.740
Excuse me! Who are you people,
and what do you want with our town?

411
00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:54.290
Oh my!

412
00:21:55.240 --> 00:21:56.450
Now, now, Morley!

413
00:21:56.450 --> 00:21:58.760
Don't have all the fun without me!

414
00:21:59.340 --> 00:22:01.590
What do you want?

415
00:22:02.600 --> 00:22:03.850
Wait a sec!

416
00:22:03.850 --> 00:22:06.060
I've got some newly-invented
weapons to try.

417
00:22:06.060 --> 00:22:08.440
Why'd you run out ahead, huh?

418
00:22:08.770 --> 00:22:10.860
Who the hell are these circus monkeys?

419
00:22:16.770 --> 00:22:18.440
Why's a murder of crows here?

420
00:22:19.230 --> 00:22:20.860
Captain!

421
00:22:20.860 --> 00:22:23.660
Look! Someone's on the roof!

422
00:22:23.660 --> 00:22:25.120
What?

423
00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:27.630
Why are the birds gathering up?

424
00:22:36.900 --> 00:22:40.980
How dare you attempt
to harm the innocent.

425
00:22:40.980 --> 00:22:44.020
Captain Peachbeard, sir?

426
00:22:44.020 --> 00:22:45.600
They shouldn't be here!

427
00:22:45.890 --> 00:22:48.640
They're supposed to be
scattered across the world!

428
00:22:51.390 --> 00:22:53.480
They're the four captains
of the Revolutionary Army!

429
00:22:54.570 --> 00:22:59.120
Wait. No way. They're what?!

430
00:23:00.030 --> 00:23:03.900
<b>Commander Morley
Eastern Division
Revolutionary Army</b>

431
00:23:00.980 --> 00:23:02.150
Knock it off.

432
00:23:02.150 --> 00:23:03.530
You're still staring!

433
00:23:04.280 --> 00:23:08.160
<b>Commander Belo Betty
Western Division
Revolutionary Army</b>

434
00:23:05.530 --> 00:23:08.030
Are y'scared yet? Scumbag.

435
00:23:08.620 --> 00:23:12.500
<b>Commander Lindbergh
Southern Division
Revolutionary Army</b>

436
00:23:09.240 --> 00:23:12.160
I'm dying to try my new weapons on you!

437
00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:17.000
<b>Commander Karasu
Northern Division
Revolutionary Army</b>

438
00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:17.080
We won't allow you to do as you please.

439
00:23:18.790 --> 00:23:22.420
Revolutionaries? Are they here to help?

440
00:23:30.390 --> 00:23:34.270
<b>Officer Emporio Ivankov
Revolutionary Army</b>

441
00:23:30.990 --> 00:23:33.540
Straw Boy really is
something else, isn't he?

442
00:23:33.830 --> 00:23:36.080
I guess the apple doesn't
fall too far from the tree!

443
00:23:34.430 --> 00:23:38.060
<b>Commander in Chief Monkey D. Dragon
Revolutionary Army</b>

444
00:23:37.170 --> 00:23:38.130
It's crazy!

445
00:23:38.670 --> 00:23:42.510
Who knew that young buck Sanji
was Germa 66's prince!

446
00:23:42.840 --> 00:23:43.970
How insolent!

447
00:23:43.970 --> 00:23:46.020
He didn't even mention it to me once.

448
00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:47.440
It pisses me off.

449
00:23:47.940 --> 00:23:49.730
As a result of that
Whole Cake incident,

450
00:23:49.730 --> 00:23:52.190
Germa's been booted from
the World Government.

451
00:23:52.830 --> 00:23:54.870
My, my, Straw Boy and Sanji Boy.

452
00:23:55.200 --> 00:23:57.080
It's just as I expected, though.

453
00:23:57.540 --> 00:24:01.500
They're becoming the center
of attention in the Great Pirate Era!

454
00:23:57.620 --> 00:24:01.500
<b>Officer Inazuma
Revolutionary Army</b>

455
00:24:01.540 --> 00:24:05.300
<b>Hack
Soldier
Revolutionary Army</b>

456
00:24:01.960 --> 00:24:05.340
I'm excited to see where this goes!

457
00:24:06.260 --> 00:24:09.340
Anyway, our officers are
running kinda late, aren't they?

458
00:24:07.010 --> 00:24:12.180
<b>Koala
Assistant Fishman Karate Instructor
Revolutionary Army</b>

459
00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:12.010
Hopefully, they didn't get held
up too bad on their way here.

460
00:24:12.300 --> 00:24:13.680
No kidding.

461
00:24:14.390 --> 00:24:15.890
By the way, Sabo.

462
00:24:15.890 --> 00:24:18.770
Whatcha got going on
over there, honey-pie?

463
00:24:20.470 --> 00:24:21.520
Lemme guess.

464
00:24:21.810 --> 00:24:23.430
Your face is cramping
because you keep smiling

465
00:24:23.430 --> 00:24:25.560
every time you think of
the Luffy news, right?

466
00:24:25.560 --> 00:24:26.770
You boob!

467
00:24:28.810 --> 00:24:29.730
Cu-lick.

468
00:24:30.270 --> 00:24:31.480
Hello, Lindbergh here!

469
00:24:31.860 --> 00:24:34.030
You guys are really late.
What's the hold up?

470
00:24:35.200 --> 00:24:37.040
Oh, hey Sabo! We are almost there.

471
00:24:37.040 --> 00:24:38.870
We ran into some trouble.

472
00:24:38.870 --> 00:24:40.710
Do you guys mind if we're a bit late?

473
00:24:41.070 --> 00:24:43.410
No problem. Just stay safe.

474
00:24:43.950 --> 00:24:45.000
Cu-lick.

475
00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:47.210
Oh, I am absolutely thrilled!

476
00:24:47.210 --> 00:24:50.960
All of the Revolutionary Army's best
will be here in the flesh at long last!

477
00:24:51.260 --> 00:24:53.930
I can't believe I'll
get to chat with Morley!

478
00:24:53.930 --> 00:24:56.020
Oh, who cares! It's all about Betty!

479
00:24:57.020 --> 00:24:59.480
Sabo. We've wasted enough time.

480
00:24:59.930 --> 00:25:01.220
We should hold our meeting now.

481
00:25:01.680 --> 00:25:04.640
We might as well solidify
our plan before they arrive.

482
00:25:04.930 --> 00:25:06.100
Looks like you're up.

483
00:25:06.100 --> 00:25:07.480
Mr. Second-in-Command.

484
00:25:07.480 --> 00:25:08.560
Yup.

485
00:25:09.230 --> 00:25:12.940
With the Reverie just round the corner,
we'll finally take action.

486
00:25:15.110 --> 00:25:17.030
We will be declaring war.

487
00:25:16.200 --> 00:25:20.710
<b>Chief of Staff Sabo
Revolutionary Army</b>

488
00:25:18.370 --> 00:25:20.120
On the Celestial Dragons.

489
00:25:22.360 --> 00:25:23.860
The Revolutionary Army.

490
00:25:24.410 --> 00:25:25.740
They're all so powerful.

491
00:25:26.570 --> 00:25:27.740
I can't believe it.

492
00:25:30.940 --> 00:25:33.950
Why are four top officers
needed to defend one town?

493
00:25:34.270 --> 00:25:36.690
Jeez! This guy is so dense!

494
00:25:36.690 --> 00:25:39.400
He only wants you
for your body, obviously.

495
00:25:39.400 --> 00:25:41.370
Ew, yuck! No thank you!

496
00:25:41.370 --> 00:25:43.910
Hey, I checked in
with Sabo like you asked.

497
00:25:43.910 --> 00:25:45.290
Can we do this now, Betty?

498
00:25:45.750 --> 00:25:47.860
You're powerless to stop us.

499
00:25:47.860 --> 00:25:50.110
Why is no one answering the question?

500
00:25:50.950 --> 00:25:53.740
And what is he mumbling about anyway?

501
00:25:53.990 --> 00:25:56.440
I've had enough of you!

502
00:25:56.440 --> 00:25:58.360
Did this guy just snap?

503
00:25:58.900 --> 00:26:01.780
Hey, you pieces of crap! Ya gonna help?

504
00:26:03.750 --> 00:26:04.880
Will you die? Or will you fight?

505
00:26:06.420 --> 00:26:09.130
It's time to choose your destiny!

506
00:26:11.800 --> 00:26:14.640
Is playing hero someone else's job?

507
00:26:18.110 --> 00:26:20.530
Are you just going to cower in fear?

508
00:26:40.730 --> 00:26:43.080
Do you really think
a couple of sticks

509
00:26:43.080 --> 00:26:44.300
are gonna stop us?

510
00:26:44.300 --> 00:26:45.880
You guys are cracking me up.

511
00:26:46.180 --> 00:26:48.590
What is this, a peasant uprising?

512
00:26:50.550 --> 00:26:51.720
I'm not sure why. But all of a sudden,

513
00:26:51.720 --> 00:26:54.420
I feel this huge surge
of power inside me!

514
00:26:54.420 --> 00:26:56.510
Yeah, let's force
these pirates to leave!

515
00:26:57.130 --> 00:26:59.300
We should fight and
protect our kingdom!

516
00:26:59.300 --> 00:27:01.170
Yeah!

517
00:27:02.340 --> 00:27:03.880
That's the stuff!

518
00:27:03.880 --> 00:27:06.640
You're feeling the raw power
of Betty's Pump-Pump Fruit!

519
00:27:06.970 --> 00:27:11.180
With a mere wave of her banner,
she can call forth the strength within you!

520
00:27:11.560 --> 00:27:14.270
Betty is a flag-bearer of freedom!

521
00:27:14.850 --> 00:27:16.980
Now! Let's go!

522
00:27:22.680 --> 00:27:25.950
Well, I guess they wanna see
what bullets do to their bodies.

523
00:27:25.950 --> 00:27:27.620
They don't know what they're in for!

524
00:27:29.880 --> 00:27:32.630
Hey Lind, Karasu! Go and back them up!

525
00:27:32.920 --> 00:27:34.000
As you wish! Now freeze!

526
00:27:35.680 --> 00:27:38.220
Cool Shooter!

527
00:27:38.970 --> 00:27:39.930
That's freezing!

528
00:27:39.930 --> 00:27:41.800
My gun got all iced up!

529
00:27:41.800 --> 00:27:44.680
How dare you attack us, you bastards!

530
00:27:47.060 --> 00:27:49.400
Don't back down! Rip 'em to shreds!

531
00:27:50.520 --> 00:27:52.020
Disarm them!

532
00:27:57.780 --> 00:27:59.740
That big bird stole our swords!

533
00:27:59.740 --> 00:28:00.910
Come back!

534
00:28:01.290 --> 00:28:02.750
It's all up to you!

535
00:28:02.750 --> 00:28:04.460
Seize your own fate!

536
00:28:04.460 --> 00:28:06.130
Now, go!

537
00:28:07.540 --> 00:28:08.920
Rot in hell!

538
00:28:14.730 --> 00:28:17.480
What is this? Why are they fired up?

539
00:28:17.480 --> 00:28:20.950
You jerk! This is for the milk!

540
00:28:45.530 --> 00:28:46.950
We're outta here!

541
00:28:46.950 --> 00:28:48.530
We'll make you pay for this!

542
00:28:50.140 --> 00:28:54.020
Peachbeard. 52 million berries, huh?

543
00:28:55.010 --> 00:28:58.470
Master Blackbeard will avenge
me, then you'll be sorry!

544
00:28:58.770 --> 00:29:02.310
I hate to break it to you, but he
doesn't give a crap about his thugs.

545
00:29:03.230 --> 00:29:05.150
Man. What's your problem?

546
00:29:05.150 --> 00:29:06.610
You're annoying.

547
00:29:06.610 --> 00:29:07.940
Agreed.

548
00:29:08.900 --> 00:29:09.900
Listen up.

549
00:29:10.190 --> 00:29:12.610
You pathetic, yellow-bellied,
weak sad sacks!

550
00:29:15.270 --> 00:29:17.900
All y'gotta do is give him
to the World Government.

551
00:29:18.160 --> 00:29:19.790
And that sweet bounty will be yours.

552
00:29:20.700 --> 00:29:23.870
That would be a total of
52 million berries.

553
00:29:24.170 --> 00:29:26.960
So. Make sure to use it wisely.

554
00:29:29.660 --> 00:29:32.170
Here. I want you to have this.

555
00:29:33.330 --> 00:29:36.250
You can use it to
contact the Revolutionary Army.

556
00:29:40.180 --> 00:29:41.930
You all made me proud today.

557
00:29:44.600 --> 00:29:46.020
Just hit us up anytime.

558
00:29:46.810 --> 00:29:48.560
When the weak stand up for themselves,

559
00:29:49.100 --> 00:29:52.150
we will always be close behind
and ready to fight.

560
00:29:54.280 --> 00:29:55.400
Ha.

561
00:30:04.520 --> 00:30:06.360
Whoa. Belo Betty rocks!

562
00:30:12.350 --> 00:30:13.970
I can't thank you enough for this.

563
00:30:13.970 --> 00:30:15.560
We'll never forget what you've done!

564
00:30:24.530 --> 00:30:25.610
Say.

565
00:30:26.190 --> 00:30:28.490
What exactly's the reason we're
meeting up with everyone anyway?

566
00:30:28.910 --> 00:30:31.490
We'll be pickin' a fight
with the Celestial Dragons.

567
00:30:31.490 --> 00:30:33.750
Oh, now that sounds like a good time!

568
00:30:33.750 --> 00:30:35.040
Heck yeah!

569
00:30:35.040 --> 00:30:36.750
Oh. One thing, Karasu!

570
00:30:37.460 --> 00:30:39.290
You need to turn up your loudspeaker.

571
00:30:42.950 --> 00:30:44.450
Sorry. Forgot.

572
00:30:46.620 --> 00:30:49.490
Only two days remain until the Reverie,

573
00:30:49.490 --> 00:30:54.120
and the schemes of players from
around the world begin to intertwine.

574
00:30:55.540 --> 00:30:57.250
Okay. Roger that.

575
00:30:57.550 --> 00:30:58.890
I have an update for you.

576
00:30:59.650 --> 00:31:02.690
Sabo? They'll be here soon.

577
00:31:03.150 --> 00:31:07.280
All right. Let's do this.

578
00:31:10.980 --> 00:31:13.230
What is this crap?

579
00:31:13.480 --> 00:31:15.400
I've seen this stupid face before!

580
00:31:15.400 --> 00:31:19.410
This is the same guy who screwed
over my entire SMILE production!

581
00:31:16.650 --> 00:31:22.150
<b>Kaido, "King of the Beasts"
One of the Four Emperors</b>

582
00:31:19.410 --> 00:31:24.080
How in the hell did he manage
to take down that old bag?

583
00:31:30.680 --> 00:31:34.690
It says "he won"? What the hell?

584
00:31:34.960 --> 00:31:37.550
When did I lose, and to whom?

585
00:31:38.300 --> 00:31:41.720
I think I know who wrote
this slanderous article, Mama!

586
00:31:41.720 --> 00:31:43.490
I do, too.

587
00:31:43.490 --> 00:31:45.830
I'll have to teach Morgans a lesson.

588
00:31:48.850 --> 00:31:51.900
But Straw Hat, you're first!

589
00:31:52.140 --> 00:31:55.270
<b>Charlotte "Big Mom" Linlin
One of the Four Emperors</b>

590
00:31:52.980 --> 00:31:55.440
I'll be coming for you!

591
00:31:57.350 --> 00:31:59.110
The Fifth Emperor?

592
00:31:57.900 --> 00:32:01.900
<b>Marshall D. "Blackbeard" Teach
One of the Four Emperors</b>

593
00:31:59.440 --> 00:32:02.360
Now that title doesn't fit you at all!

594
00:32:09.910 --> 00:32:12.660
<b>"Red-Haired" Shanks
One of the Four Emperors</b>

595
00:32:12.660 --> 00:32:15.910
Looks like I'll be seeing you soon.

596
00:32:17.710 --> 00:32:18.790
Luffy.

597
00:32:28.060 --> 00:32:31.390
So what if it got lower?
We can't do anything.

598
00:32:31.390 --> 00:32:33.400
You'll get up there again, Luffy.

599
00:32:33.400 --> 00:32:35.190
You know I got your back!

600
00:32:35.190 --> 00:32:36.650
We'll get it even higher!

601
00:32:36.650 --> 00:32:39.230
Ya hungry? I'll make lunch.

602
00:32:40.740 --> 00:32:42.110
Uh-huh.

603
00:32:46.120 --> 00:32:49.680
Uh. Just a moment.

604
00:32:49.680 --> 00:32:51.180
– Huh?
– Huh?

605
00:32:54.890 --> 00:33:00.170
Look. I believe you
missed a few zeros here, Luffy.

606
00:33:00.170 --> 00:33:04.800
Unreal.

607
00:33:04.800 --> 00:33:08.050
Your bounty's not 150 million.

608
00:33:08.050 --> 00:33:09.130
Huh?

609
00:33:10.180 --> 00:33:13.050
It's 1.5 billion!

610
00:33:20.230 --> 00:33:23.360
While the rest of the world
looks toward the Reverie,

611
00:33:23.360 --> 00:33:25.690
the Straw Hats embark
to the Land of Wano.
